On 2/5/06, James Courtier-Dutton <James@superbug.co.uk> wrote:
> On Friday 3rd Feb 2006 my house received a power surge. It destroyed a
> number of electrical items in my house.
> One was the Central Heating system, and others included all my PCs. Why
> don't surge protectors work?

Yikes! I'm sorry for the loss. It's happened to me before, spiked out
modems and ethernet cards mostly.

What type of surge protector did you use? Was it a shunt type
protector, MOV or series type? Any UPS involved? Is there any chance
you could do a small-claims court charge on your electrical utility?
Even if you can't, it's worth raising the issue with them.

jayakumar


